
### Output
The script will:
1. Display search results in the terminal with title, URL, and truncated body
2. Save results to a JSON file in the `search_results` directory with timestamp
3. Print RAG-ready formatted text to stdout

### Command Line Arguments
- `<search_query>`: The search query string (required)

### File Storage
Search results are saved in the `search_results` directory with filenames following the pattern:
`search_results_<query>_<timestamp>.json`

Each file contains:
- The original search query
- Timestamp of when the search was performed
- Count of results found
- Full list of search results with title, URL, and body
